  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "What is Lybalvi used for?",
      "a": "Lybalvi treats schizophrenia and manic or mixed episodes of bipolar I disorder and can be continued for maintenance."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why can’t I take opioids with Lybalvi?",
      "a": "Samidorphan blocks opioid receptors, which can cause withdrawal or dangerous overdose attempts if you try to overcome the blockade."
    },
    {
      "q": "Will I still gain weight?",
      "a": "You might, but studies show less weight gain than with olanzapine alone. Regular monitoring helps."
    },
    {
      "q": "How long until I feel better?",
      "a": "Some calming happens in days, but clearer improvement in psychosis or mania often takes several weeks."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is Lybalvi safe for older adults with dementia?",
      "a": "No. Like other antipsychotics, it carries a higher mortality risk and is not approved for dementia-related psychosis."
    }
